right) is the leading entry. \n\nTherefore, the leading entries of the $1$st, $2$nd, and $4$th rows of $A$ are $-3$, $4$, and $2$, respectively.\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the answer is $-3+4+2=3.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-72577/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31c3678b-4f00-54d6-bb84-c7718fd622cb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-72577"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-42024"] :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & 6 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 5 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the second row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 5 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 & 6 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 5 & 8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $B$ and $C$ are in row echelon form." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-42366/selection/e432f1020975ada4c83798ae75bfd6c0ae4dfe63215763f08b8be8ccabf8a5d3" :answer/id #uuid "6c2f1554-0fa3-55a0-9412-8f9f0d9aad8b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42366/selection/9ed3305a02906a861616af6ff886306c4a2a74885d99f506419451b33c7c9d2d" :answer/id #uuid "db2136dc-1a20-5e75-805e-a68724052a35" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42366/selection/2377e3ffc3b5cd65e1036103e0b988e5af6634b2438c63c3b7cc0592571401ab" :answer/id #uuid "a1e2e498-2e3e-5066-b0c2-3d48d6ebbb07" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42366/selection/b967c3002b3f913c5b31990d1f8159d3e1e979aa07e2842a8b67bfff1a2fd3f2" :answer/id #uuid "8a206841-44a3-5adf-95c4-44f924bc5c7a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42366/selection/e956c3af673c94782038951d8de50bf89c9a53bf4daf2ca6725a4bea4229074c" :answer/id #uuid "2fc05b75-329a-5d7f-a9d0-e87f0845a764" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42366/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "3c80ec86-b94f-53fa-b411-f4f005326625" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-42366/selection/e432f1020975ada4c83798ae75bfd6c0ae4dfe63215763f08b8be8ccabf8a5d3" :answer-field/choices ["q-42366/selection/e432f1020975ada4c83798ae75bfd6c0ae4dfe63215763f08b8be8ccabf8a5d3" "q-42366/selection/9ed3305a02906a861616af6ff886306c4a2a74885d99f506419451b33c7c9d2d" "q-42366/selection/2377e3ffc3b5cd65e1036103e0b988e5af6634b2438c63c3b7cc0592571401ab" "q-42366/selection/b967c3002b3f913c5b31990d1f8159d3e1e979aa07e2842a8b67bfff1a2fd3f2" "q-42366/selection/e956c3a