e [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-129220" :question/id #uuid "605796e6-769a-5496-86e2-e97c353a0309" :question/math-academy-id "q-129220" :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are **not** in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that a matrix is in row echelon form if it satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the first row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $A$ is **not** in row echelon form." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-129220/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d390841-351e-54f5-ad19-90b6ebae5799"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129220"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-129222/selection/9ed3305a02906a861616af6ff886306c4a2a74885d99f506419451b33c7c9d2d" :answer/id #uuid "fd2e6879-314f-574e-b6bd-5253796e4de3" :answer/type :answer.typ