ading entry of a row is in a column to the right of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -8 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 7 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 9 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ are in row echelon form." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-129228/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5d1d859-0b86-5507-a7bf-3d805a85adf3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129228"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-129231/selection/9ed3305a02906a861616af6ff886306c4a2a74885d99f506419451b33c7c9d2d" :answer/id #uuid "13d1d5a2-5e6c-538e-a669-c15b181e90c7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129231/selection/685c02320dbe687345f93d820499dea4c0c82808b910e8a0e5841f77aa82209d" :answer/id #uuid "66c670f1-6f13-5e42-9463-33a2a39c18f1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129231/selection/2377e3ffc3b5cd65e1036103e0b988e5af6634b2438c63c3b7cc0592571401ab" :answer/id #uuid "75233616-7044-5181-9bc2-905fd0bebfbe" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129231/selection/b967c3002b3f913c5b31990d1f8159d3e1e979aa07e2842a8b67bfff1a2fd3f2" :answer/id #uuid "15a73926-3c75-59fc-bfc9-8dab876dee1a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129231/selection/f073cec77042b855fcc95ae59e5c07a0d566930857e27de8effde7dcda1f144f" :answer/id #uuid "4c5958fd-106f-5f7c-b65f-6729dc4c8c8d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A,$ $B,$ and $C$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-129231/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "6f40d651-714e-50be-8b4b-f5478fe1c405" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-129231/selection/b967c3002b3f913c5b31990d1f8159d3e1e979aa07e2842a8b67bfff1a2fd3f2" :answer-field/choices ["q-129231/selection/9ed3305a02906a861616af6ff886306c4a2a74885d99f506419451b33c7c9d2d" "q-129231/selection/685c02320dbe687345f93d820499dea4c0c82808b910e8a0e5841f77aa82209d" "q-129231/selection/2377e3ffc3b5cd65e1036103e0b988e5af6634b2438c63c3b7cc0592571401ab" "q-129231/selection/b967c3002b3f913c5b31990d1f8159d3e1e979aa07e2842a8b67bfff1a2fd3f2" "q-129231/selection/f073cec77042b855fcc95ae59e5c07a0d566930857e27de8effde7dcda1f144f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-129231" :question/id #uuid "3d92198e-4ce7-5520-a0eb-698c6d6eae5d" :question/math-academy-id "q-129231" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices are **not** in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the *bottom* of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column *to the right* of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the second row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is not in row echelon form since ${b}_{33}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 & 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $A$ and $B$ are **not** in row echelon form." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-129231/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5d1d859-0b86-5507-a7bf-3d805a85adf3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-129231"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-72576/selection/e432f1020975ada4c83798ae75bfd6c0ae4dfe63215763f08b8be8ccabf8a5d3" :answer/id #uuid "c48e030a-404c-5145-a852-cf5cad4c6ccf" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72576/selection/e956c3af673c94782038951d8de50bf89c9a53bf4daf2ca6725a4bea4229074c" :answer/id #uuid "2280e6e4-61e8-5942-8c34-2b8e4964fd1f" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72576/selection/b967c3002b3f913c5b31990d1f8159d3e1e979aa07e2842a8b67bfff1a2fd3f2" :answer/id #uuid "cc675625-82fc-55f7-8a50-1d56209b88b8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ and $B$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72576/selection/685c02320dbe687345f93d820499dea4c0c82808b910e8a0e5841f77aa82209d" :answer/id #uuid "6072340e-12b7-50a7-b8cb-ade78f6cd33c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$A$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72576/selection/9ed3305a02906a861616af6ff886306c4a2a74885d99f506419451b33c7c9d2d" :answer/id #uuid "670cf066-bb39-5f2f-b241-932001a9e9bd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$B$ and $C$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-72576/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "623e785d-be8d-50ea-ade6-6cb34dfd9228" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-72576/selection/e956c3af673c94782038951d8de50bf89c9a53bf4daf2ca6725a4bea4229074c" :answer-field/choices ["q-72576/selection/e432f1020975ada4c83798ae75bfd6c0ae4dfe63215763f08b8be8ccabf8a5d3" "q-72576/selection/e956c3af673c94782038951d8de50bf89c9a53bf4daf2ca6725a4bea4229074c" "q-72576/selection/b967c3002b3f913c5b31990d1f8159d3e1e979aa07e2842a8b67bfff1a2fd3f2" "q-72576/selection/685c02320dbe687345f93d820499dea4c0c82808b910e8a0e5841f77aa82209d" "q-72576/selection/9ed3305a02906a861616af6ff886306c4a2a74885d99f506419451b33c7c9d2d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-72576" :question/id #uuid "56d36b8d-eaf9-5390-938a-e43b593b2994" :question/math-academy-id "q-72576" :question/problem "Which of the following augmented matrices are in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that an augmented matrix is in row echelon form if its coefficient matrix satisfies the following conditions:\n\n- All the zero rows (rows with only zeros), if any, are placed at the bottom of the matrix.\n- Each leading entry of a row is in a column to the right of the leading entry of the row above it.\n\nWith that in mind, let's look at each matrix in turn.\n\n- The matrix $A$ is not in row echelon form since the second row contains only zeros and it is not at the bottom of the matrix (condition I is violated).\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $B$ is in row echelon form (both conditions are satisfied).\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- The matrix $C$ is not in row echelon form since ${c}_{21}\\ne 0$ (condition II is violated).\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, only $B$ is in row echelon form." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-72576/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f5d1d859-0b86-5507-a7bf-3d805a85adf3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-72576"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-42370"] :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A$ given below.\nWhich entries of $A$ could be replaced by $0$ in order to get a matrix in row echelon form?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 7 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that by replacing ${a}_{22}$, ${a}_{32}$ and ${a}_{33}$ with $0$, we get a matrix in row echelon form:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 7 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\,⟶\\,[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe other options will not give us a matrix in row echelon form." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-42372/selection/66b1b723c06669fb2cc8497cf7756a48836a4869d8cf3fb344215c78c249d87e" :answer/id #uuid "8fb38b95-9ed9-5e36-91a3-f53c72982c81" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "${a}_{31}$ and ${a}_{41}$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42372/selection/7715cd35107bd5f2e4b67b46d48e384913c7a7c1c4b4211d3a3422c015f67245" :answer/id #uuid "39ec583c-1eec-5460-b263-c537c7b0863